# League/Org Selection in the Web App — Full Findings

## TL;DR

There is **no React Context, no localStorage, no query-param persistence**. The active league is stored **server-side on the authenticated session row** (`session.activeOrganizationId`) via **better-auth's `organization` plugin** (mapped to the `league` table). Switching a league = calling `authClient.organization.setActive(...)` (a better-auth REST endpoint, **not** a tRPC procedure), then invalidating all React Query caches. URL slug (`/leagues/$slug`) is the navigation mechanism, not the source of truth.

---

## 1. How the web app selects/keeps track of the active league/org

### The active org lives on the session (server-side)

The client reads the active league directly from the session object returned by better-auth:

`apps/web/src/routes/-components/sidebar/app-sidebar.tsx:49-51, 78-80`
```tsx
49: 	const { data: session } = authClient.useSession();
50: 	const { data: organizations } = authClient.useListOrganizations();
51: 	const { data: activeMember } = authClient.useActiveMember();
...
78: 	const activeOrg = session?.session?.activeOrganizationId
79: 		? organizations?.find((org) => org.id === session.session.activeOrganizationId)
80: 		: organizations?.[0];
```

### Switching = `setActive` in the route's `beforeLoad`

The `/leagues/$slug` route is the switching mechanism. Navigating to a league slug calls `authClient.organization.setActive({ organizationSlug })`, then invalidates **all** queries so org-scoped data refreshes:

`apps/web/src/routes/_authenticated/_sidebar/leagues/$slug/route.tsx:22-33`
```tsx
22: 		const currentActiveOrgId = session.session?.activeOrganizationId;
23: 		if (currentActiveOrgId !== org.id) {
24: 			const { error } = await authClient.organization.setActive({
25: 				organizationSlug: params.slug,
26: 			});
27: 			if (error) {
28: 				console.error("Failed to set active organization:", error);
29: 				throw redirect({ to: "/leagues" });
30: 			}
31: 			// Invalidate all queries so all org-scoped data refreshes for the new league
32: 			await context.queryClient.invalidateQueries();
33: 		}
```

### The sidebar switcher just navigates (route does the setActive)

`apps/web/src/routes/-components/sidebar/league-switcher.tsx:92-102`
```tsx
92: 	const handleTeamSelect = async (team: {...}) => {
93: 		// Navigate to the new league route - the route's beforeLoad will handle setActive
94: 		const currentPath = location.pathname;
95: 		if (currentPath.startsWith("/leagues/")) {
96: 			navigate({ to: "/leagues/$slug", params: { slug: team.plan }, replace: true });
97: 		}
98: 	};
```
The sidebar also supports `setActive` by **id** (used in the device-auth flow): `apps/web/src/routes/device/index.tsx:93-97`:
```tsx
93: 	const handleOrgSelect = async (orgId: string) => {
94: 		setSelectedOrgId(orgId);
95: 		await authClient.organization.setActive({ organizationId: orgId });
96: 		setState("approve");
97: 	};
```

### Post-login redirect to the active org

`apps/web/src/routes/index.tsx:44-45, 62-73`
```tsx
44: 	const { data: organizations, isPending: isPendingOrganizations } =
45: 		authClient.useListOrganizations();
...
62: 		if (organizations && organizations.length === 0) {
63: 			void navigate({ to: "/onboarding" });
64: 		} else if (organizations && organizations.length > 0) {
65: 			const activeOrgId = session?.session?.activeOrganizationId;
66: 			const targetOrg = activeOrgId
67: 				? (organizations.find((org) => org.id === activeOrgId) ?? organizations[0])
68: 				: organizations[0];
69: 			if (targetOrg) {
70: 				void navigate({ to: "/leagues/$slug", params: { slug: targetOrg.slug } });
71: 			}
72: 		}
```

### Client-side persistence across sign-ins (server-side, not localStorage)

Persistence is done on the **server** via the `user_preference` table, synced through better-auth `databaseHooks`:

`apps/worker/src/lib/better-auth.ts:192-233`
```ts
192: 			session: {
193: 				create: {
194: 					before: async (session) => {
195: 						if (session.activeOrganizationId) {
196: 							return;
197: 						}
198: 						const [prefs] = await db
199: 							.select({ lastActiveOrganizationId: userPreference.lastActiveOrganizationId })
200: 							.from(userPreference)
201: 							.where(eq(userPreference.userId, session.userId))
202: 							.limit(1);
203: 						if (prefs?.lastActiveOrganizationId) {
204: 							return {
205: 								data: { ...session, activeOrganizationId: prefs.lastActiveOrganizationId },
206: 							};
207: 						}
208: 					},
209: 				},
210: 				update: {
211: 					after: async (session) => {
212: 						if (session.activeOrganizationId) {
213: 							await db.insert(userPreference).values({...})
214: 								.onConflictDoUpdate({
215: 									target: userPreference.userId,
216: 									set: { lastActiveOrganizationId: session.activeOrganizationId, ... },
217: 								});
218: 						}
219: 					},
220: 				},
221: 			},
```

### The client plugin that provides all of this

`apps/web/src/lib/auth-client.ts:1-7`
```ts
1: import { passkeyClient } from "@better-auth/passkey/client";
2: import { organizationClient, adminClient } from "better-auth/client/plugins";
3: import { createAuthClient } from "better-auth/react";
4: 
5: export const authClient = createAuthClient({
6: 	plugins: [organizationClient({}), passkeyClient(), adminClient()],
7: });
```

> **Mobile gap:** `apps/mobile/src/lib/auth-client.ts:7-16` only includes `expoClient({...})` — **no `organizationClient`**. To replicate league switching on mobile you must add `organizationClient({})` from `better-auth/client/plugins`.

---

## 2. tRPC procedures for leagues/organizations

Routers are aggregated in `apps/worker/src/trpc/trpc-router.ts:16-30` under keys: `league`, `organization`, `member`, etc.

### `league.list` — list a user's leagues (with role) — `apps/worker/src/trpc/router/league-router.ts:7-25`
```ts
7: export const leagueRouter = {
8: 	list: protectedProcedure.query(async ({ ctx: { db, authentication } }) => {
9: 		const userId = authentication.user.id;
10: 
11: 		const organizations = await db
12: 			.select({
13: 				id: organization.id,
14: 				name: organization.name,
15: 				slug: organization.slug,
16: 				logo: organization.logo,
17: 				createdAt: organization.createdAt,
18: 				role: member.role,
19: 			})
20: 			.from(member)
21: 			.innerJoin(organization, eq(member.organizationId, organization.id))
22: 			.where(eq(member.userId, userId));
23: 
24: 		return { leagues: organizations };
25: 	}),
```
- Input: **none**. Output: `{ leagues: { id, name, slug, logo, createdAt, role }[] }`.

### `league.checkSlugAvailability` — `league-router.ts:27-46`
- Input: `{ slug: string }` (`z.string().min(1).max(100)`). Output: `{ slug, available: boolean }`.

### `organization.uploadLogo` / `organization.deleteLogo` — `apps/worker/src/trpc/router/organization-router.ts:20-158`
- Both use `leagueEditorProcedure` (auth + org membership + owner/editor role). Operate on `ctx.organizationId` — the active league.

### `member.list` — members of active league — `apps/worker/src/trpc/router/member-router.ts:9-56`
- Uses `activeOrgProcedure`. Input: `{ cursor?: string, limit?: number (default 10) }`. Output: `{ members: {...user nested}[], totalCount, nextCursor }`.

### No tRPC "set active league" — that's better-auth REST

There is **no tRPC procedure to switch the active league**. `setActive` is handled entirely by better-auth's organization plugin endpoint (`POST /api/auth/organization/set-active`), called via `authClient.organization.setActive({ organizationSlug | organizationId })`.

---

## 3. Database schema (leagues & orgs)

### `league` table = the "organization" (`apps/worker/src/db/schema/auth-schema.ts:95-106`)
```ts
95: export const league = sqliteTable("league", {
96: 	id: text("id").primaryKey(),
97: 	name: text("name").notNull(),
98: 	slug: text("slug").notNull().unique(),
99: 	logo: text("logo"),
100: 	createdAt: integer("created_at", { mode: "timestamp_ms" }).notNull(),
101: 	metadata: text("metadata"),
102: });
```
> better-auth's `organization` plugin is remapped to this table: `apps/worker/src/lib/better-auth.ts:284-288`:
> ```ts
> 284: 				schema: {
> 285: 					organization: {
> 286: 						modelName: "league",
> 287: 					},
> 288: 				},
> ```

### `member` table = membership (`auth-schema.ts:108-125`)
```ts
108: export const member = sqliteTable("member", {
109: 	id: text("id").primaryKey(),
110: 	organizationId: text("organization_id").notNull().references(() => league.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
111: 	userId: text("user_id").notNull().references(() => user.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
112: 	role: text("role").default("member").notNull(),
113: 	createdAt: integer("created_at", { mode: "timestamp_ms" }).notNull(),
114: });
```

### `session.activeOrganizationId` — the active-league pointer (`auth-schema.ts:41`)
```ts
41: 		activeOrganizationId: text("active_organization_id"),
```

### `invitation` table (`auth-schema.ts:127-149`) — `organizationId → league.id`, `email`, `role`, `status`, `expiresAt`, `inviterId`.

### `userPreference` table (`apps/worker/src/db/schema/user-preferences-schema.ts:5-13`)
```ts
5: export const userPreference = sqliteTable("user_preference", {
6: 	userId: text("user_id").primaryKey().notNull().references(() => user.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
10: 	defaultOrganizationId: text("default_organization_id"),
11: 	lastActiveOrganizationId: text("last_active_organization_id"),
12: 	...timestampAuditFields,
13: });
```

### League-scoped data (all FK'd to `league.id` via `leagueId`)
In `apps/worker/src/db/schema/league-schema.ts`: `player.leagueId` (line 51-53), `leagueTeam.leagueId` (76-78), `season.leagueId` (114-116). Note `player` has `userId` + `leagueId` with unique index `player_organization_user_uidx` (59-61) — a user is a "player" **per league**.

---

## 4. The "active organization" concept server-side

Yes — `activeOrgProcedure` exists. The active org is **derived from the session's `activeOrganizationId`**, not from headers/cookies directly (the cookie/session is resolved by better-auth first).

### `activeOrgProcedure` and `enforceActiveOrg` — `apps/worker/src/trpc/trpc.ts:52-64, 162`
```ts
52: const enforceActiveOrg = t.middleware(({ ctx, next }) => {
53: 	if (!ctx.authentication?.session.activeOrganizationId) {
54: 		throw new TRPCError({
55: 			code: "UNAUTHORIZED",
56: 			message: "No active league",
57: 		});
58: 	}
59: 	return next({
60: 		ctx: {
61: 			organizationId: ctx.authentication.session.activeOrganizationId,
62: 		},
63: 	});
64: });
...
162: export const activeOrgProcedure = t.procedure.use(enforceUserIsAuthed).use(enforceActiveOrg);
```

### `leagueAccessMiddleware` — validates membership + injects `ctx.organization`/`ctx.role` (`trpc.ts:71-101`)
```ts
71: const leagueAccessMiddleware = t.middleware(async ({ ctx, next }) => {
72: 	const organizationId = ctx.authentication?.session.activeOrganizationId;
73: 	if (!organizationId || !ctx.authentication) {
74: 		throw new TRPCError({ code: "UNAUTHORIZED", message: "No active league" });
75: 	}
76: 
77: 	const org = await ctx.db
78: 		.select({
79: 			id: organization.id,
80: 			slug: organization.slug,
81: 			name: organization.name,
82: 			logo: organization.logo,
83: 			role: member.role,
84: 		})
85: 		.from(organization)
86: 		.innerJoin(member, eq(member.organizationId, organization.id))
87: 		.where(and(eq(organization.id, organizationId), eq(member.userId, ctx.authentication.user.id)))
88: 		.limit(1);
89: 
90: 	if (org.length === 0) {
91: 		throw new TRPCError({ code: "NOT_FOUND", message: "League not found" });
92: 	}
93: 
